6. UNIQUE
Prevents duplicate values.
email VARCHAR(100) UNIQUE
Two employees cannot have the same email address.
7. NOT NULL
Makes a column mandatory.
employee_name VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL
You cannot insert an employee without a name.

8. DEFAULT 
DEFAULT Automatically inserts a predefined value when you don't provide one.
is_active BOOLEAN DEFAULT TRUE
If you don't provide is_active, it becomes TRUE.
9.CHECK
Validates a condition before accepting data.
salary DECIMAL(10,2) CHECK (salary > 0)
Salary must be greater than zero.

10. ON DELETE CASCADE
This is especially important when working with related tables.
Suppose a department has 10 employees. If you delete that department, what happens to its employees?
With ON DELETE CASCADE, all employees referencing that department are automatically deleted.
CREATE TABLE employees (
    employee_id INT PRIMARY KEY,
    employee_name VARCHAR(100),
    department_id INT REFERENCES departments(department_id)
    ON DELETE CASCADE
);

